  "provenance": "Finite OEM hotend replica CAD bands from https://www.printables.com/model/533213 Hotend.STEP; land radius 0.3 mm at Z=0..0.05, finite 0.25 mm bands above; retain all registered source sections. OEM assembly diagram https://wiki.bambulab.com/x1/maintenance/replace-hotend/complete-hotend-p1.jpg and assembly instructions https://wiki.bambulab.com/en/x1/maintenance/replace-hotend : ceramic heater, clip and sock hug the 7 mm hotend stem, not a 24 mm square V6 block. Sock half-extents 4.5/5.2 mm at Z=4, heater clip 4/5 at Z=5. Front housing photo https://us.store.bambulab.com/products/front-housing-assembly-p1p (P1P_2.png) shows separate narrow duct outlets and raised full-width shell. Registered stock assembly https://wiki.bambulab.com/p1/maintenance/toolhead-enclosure/front_cover_installed.jpg and https://wiki.bambulab.com/p1/maintenance/extruder-unit/hotend_installed.jpg inform positioning. Choose 70 mm full shell width, outlets at X=+-10..24 and Y=-13..5, Z=5; outer walls to X=+-30 at Z=8; risers to X=+-35 at Z=14; cover Y=-25..0 at Z=18. Photo-derived engineering estimates; the photos do not provide a dimensioned nozzle registration. No full-width skirt at Z=2 or Z=5. P1S has no X1 lidar. Carriage Y=8..33 at Z=24 follows the rod-side assembly, not Y=60. BambuStudio gantry underside 34 mm, symmetric Y span +-33 mm, infinite X. Body axial/lateral margins 0.3 mm. Nozzle-tip frame +X right, +Y rear, +Z up, mm. Best geometry estimate selected 2026-10-10; calibrated=false.",
